  SPMS FacturaCRDWS WSDL, patched for the read path. This is the file
  the module loads.

  Original: https://www.ccf.min-saude.pt/WSExternoBroker/ProxyService/FacturaCRDWS?wsdl
  A snapshot of that URL as of 2026-07-20 sits next to this file
  (FacturaCRDWS_live_20260720.wsdl). Its content is byte-for-byte what
  the CCF served, except that this repo's pre-commit hooks append the
  final newline the original lacks. To check whether SPMS changed
  anything upstream, download the URL again and diff it against the
  snapshot — the only expected artifact is the missing-final-newline
  marker on the last line. If upstream moved, re-derive this patched
  file and refresh the snapshot (new date in the name).

  Why a shipped file instead of the URL: the published WSDL cannot
  work as-is against its own service (defects below), so pointing
  zeep at the URL is not even an option; and a pinned file keeps the
  module deterministic — no runtime fetch, no surprise upstream edits.

  Three defects are fixed here relative to the snapshot, all proven
  against the live CCF (201 successful obterResultadoConferencia
  calls, 2026-08-05):

  1. obterResultadoConferencia request: the live WSDL declares an
     EMPTY sequence (no parameters at all). Added the <factura>
     element (type obterResultadoConferenciaFactura extending
     serviceMessageBase), matching the identification block the
     service actually unmarshals — the same <factura> wrapper the
     production submission envelope uses.
  2. obterResultadoConferenciaResponse: the live WSDL omits the
     JAX-WS <return> wrapper the service actually answers with.
     Added obterResultadoConferenciaResponseWrapper.
  3. Endpoint address: the live WSDL points to the internal
     http://ccfesb01prd.ccf.local:7003/... host, unresolvable from
     outside. Replaced with the public HTTPS address.

  The write operations (submeter*) are NOT patched here: this module
  only reads.
-->
